window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["23"]={"https://theconversation.com/nepal-tibet-floods-showed-the-need-for-greater-climate-finance-is-the-world-listening-294675":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"6b582fa89b46f6a36bce625b0b1518184ec067af6f65cb7973033f4778797fcf","read":"https://theconversation.com/nepal-tibet-floods-showed-the-need-for-greater-climate-finance-is-the-world-listening-294675","bytes":184513,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Nepal-Tibet floods showed the need for greater climate finance. Is the world listening?","by":[{"n":"Melanie Pill","r":"Honorary Senior Lecturer, Australian National University"}],"pub":"2026-11-11T17:29:31Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Earlier this year, a ",["massive flash flood","https://theconversation.com/nepals-flash-floods-show-the-devastating-power-of-cascading-hazards-290611"]," ripped through Nepalese and Tibetan townships along the Bhote Koshi river system, leaving more than 1,400 people dead and at least 5,000 missing."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Climate change contributed","https://theconversation.com/nepal-tibet-disaster-linked-to-climate-change-a-glaciologist-explains-290656"]," to the glacial mountain collapse that triggered the floods. But Nepal, a developing country of about 30 million people, only produces 0.05% of the world’s carbon emissions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Left with a ",["multi-billion dollar reconstruction bill","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-09-12/nepal-flood-reconstruction-cost-billions/107145518"],", Nepal is a clear-cut example of the need for greater climate finance – the funding to help developing countries protect their people and economies against climate disasters, and rebuild when they happen."]},{"k":"p","s":["But time and time again, ",["United Nations climate summits fall short","https://www.ituc-csi.org/COP29-Talks-end-with-utterly-inadequate-deal"]," of agreements that would provide enough climate finance to match the magnitude of climate change. Will COP31 be any different?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Climate disasters will send many countries into a debt spiral – but there’s a way out","https://theconversation.com/climate-disasters-will-send-many-countries-into-a-debt-spiral-but-theres-a-way-out-269318"]]},{"k":"h","s":["What is climate finance?"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Climate finance","https://unfccc.int/topics/introduction-to-climate-finance"]," is the funding that helps countries protect their people and economies from the damage wrought by global warming. It includes projects like building sea walls to protect from floods and sea-level rise, developing drought-tolerant crops or enhancing infrastructure so buildings and transport networks can withstand extreme weather. Climate finance can also fund investments that mitigate – or reduce – carbon emissions, such as renewable energy and electric transport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Since climate diplomacy began in 1995 with the first UN climate summit, developing countries – particularly ",["in the Pacific","https://theconversation.com/ahead-of-the-global-climate-summit-pacific-leaders-call-on-nations-to-keep-1-5-c-within-reach-292766"]," – have fought for greater availability of climate finance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Their argument ",["is this","https://theconversation.com/cop29-who-pays-for-climate-action-in-developing-nations-and-how-much-becomes-more-urgent-242678"],": wealthy countries should lead on climate finance because they developed with the benefit of fossil fuels, and contribute the most to climate change. In comparison, developing countries have limited resources, and emit negligible amounts of greenhouse gases but suffer disproportionate climate consequences."]},{"k":"p","s":["At the 2024 climate summit in Baku, Azerbaijan, a ",["new finance agreement","https://theconversation.com/cop29-climate-finance-deal-why-poor-countries-are-so-angry-244341"]," was reached. Developed countries committed to raise US$300 billion (A$436 billion) a year for the world’s poorest nations by 2035. This might sound ambitious, but it is nowhere near enough to address the global need."]},{"k":"p","s":["At the recent pre-COP31 talks in Fiji, Pacific leaders made it ",["abundantly clear","https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20261007-australia-touts-new-funds-for-pacific-infrastructure-at-fiji-pre-cop"]," climate finance was crucial for the survival of vulnerable countries."]},{"k":"h","s":["What is climate ‘loss and damage’?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Developing countries, such as those in the Himalayas as well as small island nations, are ",["particularly vulnerable","https://www.oecd.org/en/publications/2025/11/the-climate-action-monitor-2025_aed0c4bb/full-report/how-vulnerable-are-countries-to-climate-risks_92df65fe.html"]," to climate change because of their geographic exposure, reliance on sectors such as agriculture and lower capacity to adapt. The concept of “loss and damage” reflects the unavoidable and irreversible harm from climate change."]},{"k":"p","s":["The push to secure an official UN-backed loss and damage fund was a contentious and decades-long process, fraught with resistance from wealthy nations. So developing nations were jubilant at the close of COP27 in Eygpt in 2022, when wealthy countries finally agreed to establish a fund to respond to loss and damage."]},{"k":"p","s":["This fund made its first call for submissions at COP30 in Belém in 2025, and received almost 180 requests totalling US$2.8 billion (A$4 billion) by the June 2026 deadline. While pledges to the fund now exceed US$820 million (A$1.2 billion), there is a ",["significant financing gap","https://www.frld.org/sites/default/files/Press%20Release_Post%20B.9%20communique.pdf"]," compared to the demand."]},{"k":"p","s":["What exactly this fund will pay for, and how, is unclear. However, the catastrophe on the Nepal-Tibet border served as the first litmus test. Nepal made an urgent appeal to the fund and asked for an emergency payout of the maximum allowable amount of US$20 million (A$29 million)."]},{"k":"p","s":["At its first ever extraordinary meeting, the fund’s board decided to set aside ",["US$21.6 million","https://www.frld.org/sites/default/files/FRLD_Press_Release_Nepal_22Oct2026-2.pdf"]," (A$31 million). This is only about ",["0.7% of Nepal’s","https://www.carbonbrief.org/analysis-nepals-20m-loss-and-damage-claim-only-covers-0-7-of-flood-costs"]," actual economic loss and damage cost. And it doesn’t include non-economic losses related to health, culture or nature."]},{"k":"p","s":["The speed of that decision is historic in the notoriously snail-paced UN process. Other countries will have to wait until December 2026 for ",["the outcome of their submissions","https://www.frld.org/sites/default/files/FRLD_Press_Release_Nepal_22Oct2026-2.pdf"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["How Australia should act"]},{"k":"p","s":["As the president of COP31 negotiations, Australia’s climate minister Chris Bowen has an opportunity to elevate the topics that Turkey is strategically avoiding. These include the need for a fossil fuel phase-out – only by reducing greenhouse gas emissions can disasters such as the one in Nepal be prevented. Australia must also be an ally to island nations across the Pacific."]},{"k":"p","s":["In terms of finance, Australia should rally more support for the ",["Pacific Resilience Facility","https://forumsec.org/pacific-resilience-facility"],". This Pacific-owned and led fund acts as a self-sustaining financial model. It relied on an ",["endowment fund structure","https://forumsec.org/pacific-resilience-facility"]," designed to generate predictable, continuous returns, eliminating the need for repeating donation cycles or accumulating national debt. This fund aims to directly benefit communities on the ground, including addressing loss and damage. But it requires more long-term investment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ultimately, no amount of finance can respond to the damage that climate change is already causing across the globe. It is absolutely vital that COP31 genuinely focuses on eliminating its root cause: the human use of fossil fuels."]}],"chars":5211},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bhutan":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"09bfbfabe44a62296c079a36b96fd1fcb8aeb70b8d7d81639f4d2153c3aa0e75","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/bhutan","bytes":39005,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Bhutan travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2012-12-20T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2025-12-10T13:09:24+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bhutan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Bhutan’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Bhutan set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, see the ",["Bhutan government’s visa entry page","https://bhutan.travel/visa"]," or contact the ",["Bhutanese Embassy in Brussels","https://www.mfa.gov.bt/rbebrussels/ambassador/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you plan to leave Bhutan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to ."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual Citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to enter and leave Bhutan."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must apply for your visa in advance. The authorities will pre-approve the visa and issue it when you arrive in Bhutan."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can arrange a visa through a Bhutanese tour operator, through a Bhutanese hotel or directly through the ",["Department of Immigration’s website","https://visit.doi.gov.bt/"],". You will need to pay a non-refundable, one-off visa application fee of 40 US dollars."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling for business or other non-tourism reasons, you must arrange your visa through your sponsoring organisation in Bhutan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get your passport stamped."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure the border control officer stamps your visa in your passport."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Permits"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have permits to travel to some states in Bhutan. Your tour guide will help to get these."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you want to extend your stay in Bhutan, go to the Department of Immigration in Thimphu to make a request."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Entry and exit points"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can enter or exit Bhutan by air through the international airport in Paro, or by the land entry point in Phuentsholing."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Bhutan guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/29/bhutan"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Sustainable development fee"]},{"k":"p","s":["All adult visitors must pay a ",["daily sustainable development fee","https://bhutan.travel/visa"]," (SDF) of 100 US dollars per night. There is a lower daily charge for children. Read more ",["information about the SDF","https://bhutan.travel/visa"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Bhutan. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to take antiques out of Bhutan. Customs officials may inspect items that appear to be antiques."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking tobacco into Bhutan"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can bring a small supply of tobacco for personal use. You will need to pay taxes and duties and be able to show proof of tax and duty payments if the authorities ask you to at any point during your visit."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into or out of Bhutan"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can take up to 30,000 Bhutan ngultrum into or out of Bhutan."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to take foreign currency worth 10,000 US dollars or more into or out of Bhutan, you must declare it and get clearance from the Royal Monetary Authority of Bhutan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Indian rupees are widely accepted in Bhutan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Bhutan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Bhutan, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime levels are low across Bhutan, but you should take the same precautions as you would at home."]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep a copy of your passport’s photo page and visa, and your flight ticket separate from the originals when travelling."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bhutanese people take their customs and traditions very seriously. Respect them at all times to avoid giving offence. Particularly avoid criticising HM The King of Bhutan. If in doubt, ask your tour guide."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dress respectfully when visiting temples and Dzongs (fortified buildings, like castles), so that you do not cause offence. Your tour guide will be able to advise."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws"]},{"k":"p","s":["Alcohol is legal in Bhutan, but there are restrictions on how much alcohol tourists can buy at one time. Check with the vendor what the limit is."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Smoking and e-cigarette bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["It was illegal to sell or buy tobacco products in Bhutan until 2020. It is currently legal, but smoking is still frowned on. Be mindful of where you smoke – for example smoking near religious locations may cause offence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict penalties for possession, use and trafficking of illegal drugs. If convicted, you could get a prison sentence and heavy fine. Sentences range from a minimum of 3 years to a life sentence depending upon the type and quantity of drugs."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity was decriminalised in Bhutan in 2020, and there are no censorship laws restricting the discussion or promotion of LGBT+ topics. Same-sex marriages are not recognised. There is no legal recognition of transgender individuals."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildlife, animal products and souvenirs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Environmental conservation is critically important to Bhutan. You could be imprisoned for harming protected species. It is illegal to litter anywhere in Bhutan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"p","s":["You need to use tour guides when visiting places of interest. Otherwise, you may be refused entry."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Mountaineering and hiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["Mountaineering is banned in Bhutan, but there are trekking options across the country at a wide range of altitudes. Take advice from your tour guide."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Bhutan, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Car rentals come with a driver. If you want to drive your own vehicle, you must hire a guide to travel with you."]},{"k":"p","s":["Any car you bring into Bhutan must meet the requirements of the ",["Bhutan Road Safety and Transport Authority","https://eralis.rsta.gov.bt/"],". You must have a driving licence, insurance documents, pollution control documents and an entry permit. You will need to pay a daily charge of 4,500 ngultrum. The same fees and rules apply for motorbikes."]},{"k":"p","s":["For a stay of more than 90 days, apply for a Bhutanese driving licence from the Bhutan Road Safety and Transport Authority. You must show your UK driving licence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Car and motorbike accidents are one of the biggest causes of injury and death in Bhutan. If possible, avoid travelling at night. Always travel in a well-maintained vehicle with seatbelts."]},{"k":"p","s":["Road conditions can be dangerous, particularly in monsoon season. There are no traffic lights in Bhutan."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Weather conditions regularly affect domestic and international flights."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Monsoon"]},{"k":"p","s":["Monsoon rains can cause landslides that cut off some roads for days. Always check your route before setting off and take extra care during the monsoon season."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Several parts of Bhutan lie on active fault zones. Limited emergency vehicles, equipment and medical facilities are likely to increase the impact of an earthquake. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is high risk of wildfires, particularly in central and southern areas of the country. You will be fined if you cause a wildfire, even if it is accidental. The level of the fine increases if the wildfire is caused intentionally."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Flooding, including flash flooding, can be caused by many natural events such as monsoon rains and earthquakes. Both rural and urban areas are vulnerable."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Bhutan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/29/bhutan#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Bhutan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/29/bhutan"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Bhutan. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re carrying a large amount of medicine or medicine that’s not for your personal use, check with the ",["Bhutanese Embassy in Brussels","https://www.mfa.gov.bt/rbebrussels/ambassador/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Bhutan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Healthcare facilities vary in quality across Bhutan. One hospital (Jigme Dorji Wangchuck National Referral Hospital) in Thimphu can provide surgery and emergency treatment. Outside of Thimphu, hospitals generally provide only basic healthcare. Treatment for more complex issues is not available in Bhutan and you would need evacuation to India or Thailand for treatment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance that covers the cost of medical treatment abroad, emergency helicopter evacuation and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["English is widely spoken in Bhutan and doctors are likely to speak some English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Bhutan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 112"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 110"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 113"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["dealing with a death abroad","https://www.gov.uk/after-a-death/death-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["being arrested or imprisoned","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/arrested-or-detained-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/bhutan/british-high-commission-kolkata"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bhutan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":12307,"change":"New information about dual nationals returning to the UK (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/peak-polycrisis-why-trumps-midterm-drubbing-gives-us-reason-for-cautious-hope-296192":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"ce1d5a00c890c6df205430b96f8792adc9aa9e5eaa8d3184e1a1434337c2bb8e","read":"https://theconversation.com/peak-polycrisis-why-trumps-midterm-drubbing-gives-us-reason-for-cautious-hope-296192","bytes":189581,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Peak polycrisis? Why Trump’s midterm drubbing gives us reason for cautious hope","by":[{"n":"Andrew Heffernan","r":"Climate Associate at the Information Integrity Lab and Adjunct Professor in Political Studies, L’Université d’Ottawa/University of Ottawa"}],"pub":"2026-11-10T12:57:13Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["For the better part of a decade, reading the news has felt like watching a pile-up in slow motion. A pandemic. Wars in Ukraine, Gaza and Sudan. A cost-of-living squeeze that never quite eases. Wildfire smoke settling over Canadian cities. And the climate numbers keep setting records nobody wanted: according to the EU’s Copernicus service, 2023 to 2025 was ",["the first three-year stretch to average more than 1.5 C above pre-industrial levels.","https://www.rte.ie/news/world/2026/0114/1552984-climate-change-report"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Scholars have a word for this tangle of overlapping, mutually reinforcing shocks: the polycrisis. It’s an accurate and exhausting word."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["‘Polycrisis’ may be a buzzword, but it could help us tackle the world’s woes","https://theconversation.com/polycrisis-may-be-a-buzzword-but-it-could-help-us-tackle-the-worlds-woes-195280"]]},{"k":"p","s":["So let me say something in the aftermath of the midterm elections in the United States that may sound naive. I think we may have passed peak polycrisis."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Not because the problems are going away","https://theconversation.com/el-nino-2026-27-as-a-polycrisis-what-happens-when-health-and-energy-systems-fail-simultaneously-294109"],". Most of them will get worse. Climate change does not negotiate, wars do not end on schedule and the next pandemic is a question of when. What I think may have peaked is something else: the political dysfunction that made all of this so much harder to govern."]},{"k":"h","s":["A long view of bad times"]},{"k":"p","s":["Humans have always lived with shocks they did not choose. Plague, famine, war, depression. What has varied across history is whether societies could pull together to manage them. The institutions built after the Second World War in 1945 were not designed by people who thought the world was safe. They were designed by people who had just seen how bad things could get and decided co-operation was worth the trouble."]},{"k":"p","s":["That capacity to work together is precisely what’s eroded over the past decade. Right-wing populism spread across democracies by turning frustration into grievance, and grievance into contempt for experts, institutions and anyone on the other side."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["The ‘freedom convoy’ protesters are a textbook case of ‘aggrieved entitlement’","https://theconversation.com/the-freedom-convoy-protesters-are-a-textbook-case-of-aggrieved-entitlement-176791"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Trust collapsed. This year’s Edelman Trust Barometer found that ",["70 per cent of people worldwide are unwilling or hesitant to trust someone with different values.","https://www.edelman.com/news-awards/2026-edelman-trust-barometer-society-slides-into-insularity"]," In Canada, the figure is 73 per cent, and only 16 per cent of Canadians expect the next generation to be better off."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s impossible to govern a polycrisis under those conditions. Climate policy, pandemic preparedness and trade all depend on people accepting a shared set of facts and accepting that losing an argument is not the end of the world. Populism attacks both requirements."]},{"k":"h","s":["Global shifts"]},{"k":"p","s":["Which is why the U.S. midterms matter. American voters handed President Donald Trump a sweeping rebuke, ",["giving Democrats control of both the House and the Senate.","https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/election-day-2026-midterms/"]," Democrats flipped at least seven Senate seats, including Ohio, North Carolina, Iowa and even Kansas and South Carolina. Susan Collins lost her Senate seat in Maine, and in Texas of all places, James Talarico beat Ken Paxton. With races in Alaska and Mississippi still too close to call, ",["Democrats will hold at least 54 Senate seats.","https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/senate-election-results-2026/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["One midterm, on its own, proves little. The president’s party usually loses ground. But this one doesn’t stand alone."]},{"k":"p","s":[["In April, Hungarians ended Viktor Orbán’s 16 years in power","https://www.rferl.org/a/hungarian-opposition-leader-magyar-landslide-victory-orban/33730633.html"],", giving Péter Magyar’s Tisza party 53.6 per cent of the vote to the Fidesz party’s 37.8. Orbán was never just another populist. He was the model, the leader the international right flew to Budapest to learn from."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Lula da Silva also defeated Flávio Bolsonaro in the recent presidential runoff","https://kuwaittimes.com/article/52394/world/lula-wins-4th-term-as-flavio-bolsonaro-vows-to-seek-annulment/"],", 51.8 to 48.2 per cent."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Hungary turns the page into uncertainty after Péter Magyar ends Viktor Orbán’s enduring rule","https://theconversation.com/hungary-turns-the-page-into-uncertainty-after-peter-magyar-ends-viktor-orbans-enduring-rule-280656"]]},{"k":"p","s":["In Britain, Reform UK looked unstoppable a year ago. Since ",["Andy Burnham replaced Keir Starmer as prime minister this summer","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/9/30/burnham-bounce-why-labours-rising-again-reforms-slipping"],", Labour led every voting intention poll conducted in October, while ",["Reform slid from around 30 per cent to roughly 22.","https://leftfootforward.org/2026/11/labour-lead-every-single-opinion-poll-carried-out-in-october/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["In Israel, ",["Benjamin Netanyahu’s long hold on power may finally be slipping","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/29/israel-election-result-shows-no-overall-majority-as-vote-count-complete"],". His right-wing and religious bloc fell short of a majority in the recent election, winning only 53 of 120 seats, while Arab-led parties won a record 19."]},{"k":"p","s":["When President Isaac Herzog consulted the new Knesset, ",["67 lawmakers recommended challenger Gadi Eisenkot and only 46 backed Netanyahu","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/7/israels-president-picks-eisenkot-over-netanyahu-to-form-next-government"],", and Herzog gave Eisenkot the first chance to form a government."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Can Gadi Eisenkot turn the ‘disaster bloc’ into Israel’s next government?","https://theconversation.com/can-gadi-eisenkot-turn-the-disaster-bloc-into-israels-next-government-295859"]]},{"k":"p","s":["And in Canada, ",["Mark Carney’s approval sits at 65 per cent","https://press.liaisonstrategies.ca/federal-tracker-liberal-lead-narrows-to-13-points-october-26-2026/"],", a remarkable number for a prime minister a year and a half into the job. Opposition leader Pierre Poilievre, whose brand rests on the claim that Canada is broken, is viewed unfavourably by 52 per cent of Canadians in the same poll."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a pattern here. After a decade of rage politics, voters in very different countries seem to be reaching again for competence and something closer to normal."]},{"k":"h","s":["Taking on the social media accelerant"]},{"k":"p","s":["Something else has changed too. The platforms that pour fuel on the polarization flames no longer operate in a regulatory vacuum."]},{"k":"p","s":["Late ",["last year, the European Commission fined social media platform X 120 million euros for breaching its transparency obligations","https://ec.europa.eu/commission/presscorner/detail/en/ip_25_2934"],", the first penalty issued under the Digital Services Act."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Australia’s restrictions on social media accounts for those under 16 years old have been in force since December 2025","https://esafety.gov.au/about-us/industry-regulation/social-media-age-restrictions"],". After years of hearings and white papers, regulating big tech has moved from talk to enforcement."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Australia’s social media ban has an enforcement problem. These new laws aim to fix it","https://theconversation.com/australias-social-media-ban-has-an-enforcement-problem-these-new-laws-aim-to-fix-it-291356"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Hope, with fine print"]},{"k":"p","s":["None of this calls for a victory lap."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Brazil, ",["Lula won by under four points, and his opponent has vowed to seek an annulment","https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/10/25/world/brazil-election"],". In the U.K., Reform still polls above 20 per cent and ",["some predict the Burnham bounce will fade","https://www.telegraph.co.uk/politics/2026/10/27/hundred-days-andy-burnham-bounce-peaked/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Trump remains president for two more years, veto pen in hand, and ",["has made the most fiery hardliner in his administration, Stephen Miller","https://www.ctvnews.ca/world/article/trump-replaces-susie-wiles-with-stephen-miller-as-chief-of-staff-after-gops-midterm-defeat/"],", his chief of staff."]},{"k":"p","s":["The grievances that populists exploited are real and unresolved: housing, wages, the sense of being left behind. And the polycrisis carries on regardless of who wins elections."]},{"k":"p","s":["Cautious optimism is still optimism, though. The shocks may not be over, but our ability to respond to them, together, may be returning. ",["Historically, like in the post-Second World War period, that’s mattered most","https://psyche.co/ideas/from-wars-to-pandemics-people-in-crisis-need-to-feel-connected"]," during crises."]},{"k":"p","s":["For those of us who work on democracy, information integrity and multilateral co-operation, this is no time to ease off. It is a moment to press the advantage: to rebuild trust, shore up the institutions that let us govern shared problems and make the case once more that working together beats tearing each other apart."]},{"k":"p","s":["The problems are not getting smaller. But for the first time in a while, we may be getting better at facing them."]}],"chars":6651},"https://theconversation.com/pejabat-bukan-gen-alpha-asbun-mereka-saat-asap-karhutla-bukan-salah-ucap-tapi-krisis-empati-294869":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"6564157f856d755a687bcc6c462b6e3c2c8386f8954e2dfae372926d21449c30","read":"https://theconversation.com/pejabat-bukan-gen-alpha-asbun-mereka-saat-asap-karhutla-bukan-salah-ucap-tapi-krisis-empati-294869","bytes":177808,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Pejabat bukan Gen Alpha: ‘Asbun’ mereka saat asap karhutla bukan salah ucap, tapi krisis empati","by":[{"n":"Khairani","r":"Lecturer and Researcher, Member of Digital Services Marketing Research Cluster FEBUI, Universitas Indonesia"},{"n":"Inta Hartaningtyas Rani","r":"Dr./ Manajer Riset dan Media CHED ITB Ahmad Dahlan, Institut Teknologi dan Bisnis Ahmad Dahlan"}],"pub":"2026-11-03T04:00:41Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["● Pejabat daerah gagal menunjukkan empati dan keseriusan dalam merespons krisis karhutla."]},{"k":"p","s":["● Lelucon di tengah bencana merusak kepercayaan publik terhadap pemerintah."]},{"k":"p","s":["● Komunikasi krisis harus mengutamakan keselamatan, empati, dan kredibilitas informasi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kabut asap kembali menyelimuti sebagian Sumatra dan Kalimantan. Di Kotawaringin Barat, Kalimantan Tengah, BMKG setempat mencatat kualitas udara masuk ",["kategori sangat berbahaya","https://www.antaranews.com/berita/5770688/bmkg-sebut-kualitas-udara-di-palembang-di-level-sangat-berbahaya"],". Warga mengeluhkan sesak napas, batuk, dan mata perih."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di tengah situasi itu, Gubernur Kalimantan Tengah Agustiar Sabran justru melontarkan pelesetan ",["“bersatu kita teguh, bercerai kita kawin lagi”","https://news.detik.com/berita/d-8704537/pkb-kritik-gubernur-kalteng-bercanda-bercerai-kawin-lagi-soal-karhutla"]," saat ditanya soal penanganan kebakaran hutan dan lahan (karhutla)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di Sumatra Selatan, Wali Kota Palembang Ratu Dewa, menanggapi pertanyaan soal kondisinya di tengah asap dengan menjawab ",["“mungkin saya enjoy-enjoy aja”","https://www.detik.com/sumbagsel/berita/d-8691515/ratu-dewa-sebut-asap-di-palembang-kiriman-dari-ogan-ilir-OKI-dan-banyuasin"],". Padahal kondisi di Palembang juga parah, ",["BMKG mencatat","https://www.bmkg.go.id/kualitas-udara/pm25/pm25_pl3"]," konsentrasi PM2.5 mencapai 554 µg/m³ pada 5 Oktober 2026, lebih dari dua kali ambang kategori berbahaya. Bahkan hingga 20 Oktober 2026, asap pekat masih mengepung Kota Palembang."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ucapan di atas kerap kita kenal sebagai ‘asbun’, alias asal bunyi yang mudah dianggap sebagai keseleo lidah. Namun, dalam kacamata komunikasi krisis, asbun adalah kegagalan komunikasi publik."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam situasi darurat, pejabat merupakan bagian dari komunikasi krisis yang seharusnya membantu warga memahami bahaya dan melindungi diri, bukan melontarkan lelucon."]},{"k":"h","s":["Humor yang salah tempat"]},{"k":"p","s":["Teori ",["Situational Crisis Communication (SCCT)","https://link.springer.com/article/10.1057/palgrave.crr.1550049"]," menyebutkan bahwa respons pihak berwenang harus sepadan dengan tingkat tanggung jawab yang dilekatkan publik kepadanya. Berdasarkan teori tersebut, prioritas pertama dalam krisis adalah melindungi warga dari bahaya, bukan menjaga citra organisasi—dalam konteks ini atau pemerintah."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pemerintah seharusnya mengarahkan masyakarat agar bisa melindungi diri (instructing information). Misalnya menghimbau penggunaan masker, atau ungkapan kepedulian bagi warga yang terdampak. Bukan asal menyeletuk dengan dalih melucu."]},{"k":"p","s":["Karhutla bukan kejadian baru, bencana ini berulang hampir setiap kemarau dan sudah seharusnya bisa dicegah atau diredam dampaknya baik oleh pemerintah daerah ataupun pemerintah pusat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam SCCT, krisis yang bisa dicegah dan punya riwayat berulang menuntut strategi membangun kembali (rebuild): mengakui masalah, menunjukkan kepedulian, dan menjelaskan tindakan perbaikan. Jawaban ‘asbun’ justru menunjukkan sikap menyangkal (denial) atau mengecilkan (diminish) masalah."]},{"k":"p","s":["Padahal, ",["penelitian tahun 2020","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33132966/"]," menunjukkan bahwa penanganan krisis yang efektif sangat membutuhkan keyakinan warga bahwa pemerintah mampu melindungi mereka."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di Indonesia, pola komunikasi yang buruk memang terus berulang. Saat pandemi COVID-19, Menteri Kesehatan kala itu, Terawan Agus Putranto, mengatakan “enjoy saja, makan yang cukup”. ",["Riset tahun 2022","https://journal.ugm.ac.id/jsp/article/view/66443"]," tentang bagaimana komunikasi pemerintah Indonesia selama pandemi COVID-19 mencatat narasi pemerintah saat itu cenderung menyepelekan ancaman."]},{"k":"p","s":["Riset tersebut juga menggolongkan metafora pejabat yang merendahkan sebagai bad language, yaitu bahasa yang lahir dari pola pikir buruk dan berpotensi menyakiti. Pelesetan “bersatu kita teguh, bercerai kita kawin lagi” masuk dalam pola yang sama."]},{"k":"h","s":["Apa yang perlu dibenahi?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Komunikasi krusial dalam manajemen krisis, termasuk krisis kesehatan. Pusat Pengendalian dan Pencegahan Penyakit Amerika Serikat (Centers for Disease Control and Prevention/CDC) menyediakan pelatihan khusus Crisis and Emergency Risk Communication (CERC). Pelatihan ini ditujukan tidak hanya kepada tenaga kesehatan, tetapi juga kepada para pemimpin agar dapat berkomunikasi dengan baik dalam kondisi bahaya dan darurat."]},{"k":"p","s":["CERC juga memberikan panduan bagaimana berinteraksi dengan media, di antaranya be first (terdepan), be right (terbenar), dan be credible (terpercaya). Jawaban ‘asbun’ jelas tidak sesuai dengan panduan ini dan hanya akan membuat masyarakat meragukan kredibilitas penanganan krisis dan bencana."]},{"k":"p","s":["Padahal, Pasal 26 ayat 1 ",["UU Penanggulangan Bencana","https://peraturan.bpk.go.id/Details/39901/uu-no-24-tahun-2007"]," menempatkan rasa aman dan akses terhadap informasi kebijakan penanggulangan bencana sebagai hak setiap orang, bukan hadiah penguasa."]},{"k":"p","s":[["UU Keterbukaan Informasi Publik","https://jdih.komdigi.go.id/produk_hukum/view/id/172/t/undangundang%2Bnomor%2B14%2Btahun%2B%2B2008%2Btanggal%2B30%2Bapril%2B2008?search=permendagri+perlindungan+data+pribadi&utm_source=chatgpt.com"]," juga menegaskan: ketika ada ancaman terhadap hajat hidup orang banyak, badan publik wajib mengumumkannya serta-merta, dengan bahasa yang mudah dipahami ."]},{"k":"p","s":["Maka, ketika wartawan bertanya soal karhutla, yang berhak didengar warga adalah status bahaya, langkah penanganan, dan cara melindungi diri. Lelucon asbun tidak memuat satu pun dari ketiganya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Komunikasi krisis harus jujur, terbuka, cepat, akurat, dan lengkap. Sikap menyangkal atau mengecilkan krisis justru menggerus kredibilitas dan memperbesar dampak buruknya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Saat krisis, warga butuh informasi agar bisa bertindak tepat: cara menghindari bahaya, gejala yang perlu diwaspadai, dan ke mana harus berobat. Pemerintah perlu menunjuk juru bicara dan kanal resmi sejak awal, sekaligus menyampaikan empati kepada masyarakat, bukan melontarkan lelucon asbun."]}],"chars":4978},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/comoros":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"c9731b46a73e66fe60deae059371fa238f2c0524da72e6294f4ec548c569e5d7","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/comoros","bytes":40220,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Comoros travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2012-12-18T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2025-12-10T13:42:55+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/comoros/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Comoros’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Comoros set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the Comoros Embassy in Paris (in French)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Comoros, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to enter or travel through Comoros. You can buy a visa for 30 euros when you arrive at Hahaya airport or other points of entry."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Comoros guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/54/comoros#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Comoros","https://douane.gov.km/en/dedouanement.php"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Comoros"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Comoros, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests and unrest can happen in Comoros, including in Moroni and other parts of Grande Comore, Anjouan and Mohéli, particularly following elections. Protests have previously blocked roads, making travel in Moroni difficult, including between the city and the international airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["In January 2024, a protestor was killed and several injured in clashes with security forces."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid crowds and demonstrations and follow the advice and instructions of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Due to a longstanding dispute between Comoros and France about the island of Mayotte, there is some anti-French sentiment in Comoros and occasional demonstrations on the issue. Monitor local media to keep up to date with developments."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime levels are low but take precautions against pickpocketing. Street crime such as robbery is rare. Walking alone at night increases your risk, including on beaches or in town centres."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep your valuables, cash and important documents in hotel safes where possible."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always travel with your ID. Keep printed copies of your passport’s photo page and visa stamp."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Religion"]},{"k":"p","s":["Comoros is an Islamic country. The official religion is Sunni Islam. People are not allowed to practise Shia Islam in Comoros."]},{"k":"p","s":["Respect local traditions, customs, laws and religious practices. Make sure you do not offend cultural or religious beliefs."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress and behaviour codes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Clothing for men and women needs to cover the body loosely, from the shoulders to the knees."]},{"k":"p","s":["Islanders mostly consider outward displays of intimacy to be contrary to public decency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["All matters of religious practice and custom are given particular importance by the people and authorities throughout the year. This importance is especially heightened during the month of Ramadan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. Check the year’s Ramadan dates before you travel. During this time of Ramadan do not:"]},{"k":"li","s":["eat, drink, smoke or chew gum in public in the daytime, including in your car or in public view"]},{"k":"li","s":["play loud music or dance"]},{"k":"li","s":["swear in public"]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that if hotels and restaurants are providing food or drink in fasting hours, they may separate you from Islamic guests, for example with screens"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local dress codes – clothing that does not meet local dress codes may cause more offence at this time"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that fasting can cause tiredness, particularly during the later afternoon and early evening"]},{"k":"li","s":["be patient and show tolerance"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is possible to buy alcohol in Comoros, for example at hotels, but drinking alcohol or being drunk on public highways is illegal. Offences are punishable by fines or even imprisonment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pay particular attention to these rules during the Ramadan period."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drug trafficking and possession are serious offences. If you are found guilty, you could get a long prison sentence and a fine."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is advisable to ask people for permission before photographing them. Avoid taking photos of public buildings, particularly military and police buildings."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is illegal in Comoros. If convicted you could get a prison sentence of up to 5 years and heavy fines."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are very few banks or ATMs in Grande Comore or on the other islands. People in Comoros mainly use cash. Credit cards are not always accepted – check in advance if your hotel accepts your card."]},{"k":"p","s":["Technical or connection issues with equipment may also make it difficult to pay by card so always have cash available. Some hotels and restaurants accept foreign currencies such as euros. However, they will give you change in Comorian francs."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Comoros, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Comoros for up to 3 months. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need an extension after 3 months, go to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs at Rue du place de l’indépendance des Comores à Moroni or visit their Facebook page: ",["Ministère des Affaires Etrangères de l’Union des Comores","https://www.facebook.com/people/Minist%C3%A8re-des-Affaires-Etrang%C3%A8res-de-lUnion-des-Comores/100064519133618/?mibextid=ZbWKwL"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["On Grande Comore, the main ring-road is of a reasonable standard, but many other roads are in poor condition."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Boats and ferries take passengers between the 3 islands. They can be overloaded, in poor condition and without life jackets. Overloaded vessels have capsized in Comorian waters with significant loss of life."]},{"k":"p","s":["Recent attacks off the coast of Somalia and the Gulf of Aden highlight the significant risk of piracy and armed robbery."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling by sea, ",["read about the regional risks at sea","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tropical cyclones"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tropical cyclones can affect Comoros between January and May. Monitor local news and check ",["World Meteorological Organization weather reports for Comoros","https://severeweather.wmo.int/tc/swi/index.html"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Volcanic eruptions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Karthala, near Moroni on Grande Comore, is an active volcano which last erupted in 2007. Check ",["Karthala’s most recent reports and monitoring","https://volcano.si.edu/volcano.cfm?vn=233010"]," before you make plans to visit."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call hospitals and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"li","s":["Grande Comore, hopital El Maarouf: +269 773 26 04"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mohéli, hopital de Fomboni: +269 772 03 73"]},{"k":"li","s":["Anjouan, hopital de Hombo: +269 771 00 34"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Comoros","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/54/comoros#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Comoros","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/54/comoros"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Comoros"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities on all 3 islands of Comoros are basic and most are private. Disruptions to electricity and water supplies can affect hospitals and other public services."]},{"k":"p","s":["Makes sure you have adequate travel insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical facilities in Comoros","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/comoros-doctors"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Comoros"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 113 or 114"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 117"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/what-to-do-after-a-british-national-dies-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/arrested-or-detained-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/comoros/british-embassy-antanarivo"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/comoros/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":11457,"change":"New information about dual nationals returning to the UK (‘Entry requirements’ page)."}};
